@startuml 3.9-cryptographic-boundaries
skinparam handwritten false
skinparam monochrome true
skinparam defaultFontName "Arial"
skinparam shading false

title AdriaBOX - Cryptographic Horizons and Separation Boundaries

box "Tenant User Space Boundary\n(Max / Sam)" #White
participant "Client CLI\n(cli.py)" as CLI
participant "Crypto Engine\n(crypto.py)" as Crypto
participant "Transfer Manager\n(transfer.py)" as TM
end box

box "Metadata Control Plane (HTTPS)" #White
participant "Metadata Server\n(server.py / Flask)" as Master
database "SQLite DB\n(metadata.db)" as DB
end box

box "Decentralized Data Plane" #White
participant "Storage Node\n(node.py)" as Node
end box

== PHASE 1: Control Plane Handshake (HTTPS Layer) ==
CLI -> Master: HTTP POST /login (Username, Password via TLS/HTTPS Envelope)
activate Master
note left: HTTPS protects the wire\nagainst sniffing during transit
Master -> DB: verify user hash via Werkzeug
DB --> Master: yield payload context
Master -> Master: compile signed JWT Token
CLI <-- Master: HTTP 200 OK (Delivers JWT via HTTPS)
deactivate Master

== PHASE 2: Local Key Derivation (Zero-Knowledge Layer) ==
CLI -> Crypto: derive_key(password, salt=username)
activate Crypto
note over Crypto: Executes 100,000 PBKDF2 iterations\nLocal RAM computation only
Crypto --> CLI: 256-bit AES Symmetric Key (Base64)
deactivate Crypto
note over CLI: Key NEVER leaves the user machine.\nMaster Server remains completely blind.

== PHASE 3: Data Plane Transfer (End-to-End Encrypted Payload) ==
CLI -> TM: upload(file_path, plan)
activate TM
TM -> Crypto: get_stream_cipher(chunk_filename)
Crypto --> TM: AES-256-CTR Cipher Instance

loop For each 4KB User-Space Staging Buffer
    TM -> TM: Read 4KB Plaintext from SSD
    TM -> TM: Encrypt 4KB block in-place -> Ciphertext
    TM -> Node: Stream 4KB Ciphertext fragment via Raw TCP Socket
    activate Node
    Node -> Node: Write raw bytes directly to disk volume
    deactivate Node
end
note over Node: Physical storage files\ncontain exclusively ciphertext
TM --> CLI: Upload pipeline confirmation status
deactivate TM
@enduml
